From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qosify: start an interface anew on a replaced device

When pppoe-wan goes away and comes back before qosify checks it, as when
its PPP session ends and a new one starts while the hotplug events wait
their turn, qosify takes the new device for the one it set up, and
leaves it without shaping or classification.

Carry the qosify patch that remembers the device an interface was set
up on, and starts the interface anew on any other.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/network/config/qosify/Makefile        |  2 +-
 ...-interface-anew-on-a-replaced-device.patch | 92 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/network/config/qosify/patches/100-interface-start-an-interface-anew-on-a-replaced-device.patch

